Description: Leave horizontal scroll events unhandled when tab scrolling is disabled
 With gtk-horizontal-tab-scroll disabled, the sideways part of a scroll is
 forwarded to the terminal and the event was then reported to GTK as handled.
 During a diagonal TrackPoint or touchpad scroll this blocked the vertical
 scrolling of the surface. The event is now reported as unhandled after the
 forwarding, as proposed upstream in pull request 14401, which was closed
 unreviewed by the vouch bot.
--- a/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig
+++ b/src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig
@@ -3159,7 +3159,9 @@
             return @intFromBool(false);
         };

-        return @intFromBool(true);
+        // reported as unhandled: a handled sideways event blocked the vertical
+        // scrolling of the surface during a diagonal scroll
+        return @intFromBool(false);
     }

     fn ecMouseScrollHorizontalReset(ud: ?*anyopaque) callconv(.c) c_int {
